==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-run through.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|<,,ran,run>}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic}} To [[repeat]] something.
#: {{syn|en|reiterate|run back}}
#: {{ux|en|We will '''run through''' scene 2 until we get it right.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic}} To [[summarise]] [[briefly]].
##: {{syn|en|run over|sum up|Thesaurus:recapitulate}}
##: {{ux|en|Let me '''run through''' today's meeting for those who missed it.}}
##* {{quote-book
|en
|year=2003
|author=Joe Kraynak
|title=The complete idiot's guide to computer basics
|page=145
|passage=The following steps '''run''' you '''through''' a typical scanning operation using a flatbed scanner: ...}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic}} To [[go through]] [[hastily]].
#: {{syn|en|skim through|slubber}}
#: {{ux|en|to '''run through''' a book}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic|colloquial}} To quickly [[inform]], [[train]] or [[educate]] someone, typically of a new [[concept]] or a concept particular to an organization or industry.
##* {{quote-book
|en
|year=2009
|author=Jorge S. Olson
|coauthors=Carlos Lopez
|title=Build Your Beverage Empire
|page=115
|passage=... we'll '''run''' you '''through''' a very quick and abbreviated process from production through bottling.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To get something approved quickly.
##: {{ux|en|The plans for the new building were '''rushed through'''.}}
## {{senseid|en|use up, expend}} {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic}} To [[use]] (something, often money) completely, in a short space of time.
##: {{syn|en|eat up|expend}}
##: {{nearsyn|en|burn through|get through<id:use up, expend>}}
##: {{ux|en|I '''ran through''' my wages in two days. Now I've got to live on next to nothing till Friday!}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic}} To [[pervade]], of a [[quality]] that is [[characteristic]] of a group, organisation, or system.
#: {{syn|en|permeate|riddle}}
#: {{ux|en|Fear of foreigners '''runs through''' that country at all levels of its society.}}
#* {{RQ:FT|date=2019-07-11|author=John Thornhill|title=Does tech threaten to rerun the worst of the Industrial Revolution?|url=https://www.ft.com/content/f1b84f22-a25b-11e9-974c-ad1c6ab5efd1|passage=The central concern that '''runs through''' ''The Technology Trap'' is that, unless we are very careful, our latest technological revolution may well turn out to be a tumultuous rerun of the Industrial Revolution, with dire social and political consequences.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|of a flavor or ingredient}} To be present and intense.
##: {{ux|en|The cardamom '''runs through''' the cake.}}
# ''Senses as to continuing all the way through something''
## {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic}} To [[impale]] (a person) with a blade, usually a sword.
##: {{syn|en|spear|transpierce|Thesaurus:impale|Thesaurus:stab}}
##: {{ux|en|Make just one move, and I'll '''run''' you '''through''', sir, without hesitation.}}
##* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1676
|author=Thomas Shadwell
|title=The libertine: a tragedy : acted by His Royal Highness's servants
|page=15
|passage=''D. Lop."'' Offer to flinch, and I'll '''run you through'''. ''Offic.:'' Take their Swords, or knock 'em down.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|figurative|slang}} To [[have sex]] with (someone).
##: {{syn|en|fuck|plough|service|Thesaurus:copulate with}}
##* {{quote-book|en
|url=https://books.google.ch/books?id=FEonEAAAQBAJ&pg=PT16
|title=Jukes & Tonks: Crime Fiction Inspired by Music in the Dark and Suspect Choices
|author=Trey R. Barker; Jonathan Brown; S.A. Cosby; John M. Floyd; Debra H. Goldstein; Gar Anthony Haywood; Penny Mickelbury; William Dylan Powell; Kimberly B. Richardson; Stacy Woodson
|publisher=Down & Out Books
|date=2021-04-19
|passage=“There's a white girl, Betty Anderson, down on Cricket Hill Lane parked under them mulberry trees across from the old Carter place getting '''run through''' by a colored boy in a bright red Plymouth Fury. You might wanna get out there before Big Jim Anderson find{{sic}} himself with a half-breed grandchild,” {{...}}
}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic}} To continue past an intersection or a sign that is intended to cause one to stop.
##: {{ux|en|You just '''ran through''' a stop sign.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|of a waterway}} To [[flow]] through an [[area]].
##: {{ux|en|The Seine river '''runs through''' Paris.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive|of a train}} To have a route that goes through an area; to continue through an area; to complete a route.
##: {{ux|en|This train '''runs through''' the county.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|of a train}} To continue through territory owned by another company without being exchanged for a different train.
## {{lb|en|historical|metalworking}} To produce steel by continuing to pump molten iron into a [[mould]] after it is full.
# {{&lit|en|run|through}}
#: {{ux|en|He '''ran through''' the park to get the other side.}}

====Usage notes====
* The verb and particle are inseparable except in sense 7. (''impale with a sword'')

